1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,080
Ten centuries before the cross, a song recorded

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:05,660
exactly how a dying man's clothes would be

3
00:00:05,660 --> 00:00:06,300
divided up.

4
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:08,320
Psalm 22.

5
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:12,560
David wrote it in the first person, but David

6
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,080
himself was never executed.

7
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:16,060
He died an old man.

8
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:18,740
He was describing someone else.

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,320
Stripped, surrounded, his life poured out.

10
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:25,580
Watch one line.

11
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:28,600
He wrote that the dying man's killers would

12
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:31,420
divide his clothes and cast lots for them.

13
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:35,400
They part my garments among them and cast lots

14
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:36,900
upon my vesture.

15
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:39,580
A thousand years later, John watched it at

16
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:42,980
the cross, soldiers dividing Jesus's clothes,

17
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:53,120
then casting lots for

18
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:53,420
the seamless coat, that the scripture might

19
00:00:53,313 --> 00:00:53,613
be fulfilled.

20
00:00:53,318 --> 00:00:53,618
A thousand years early, God had it written

21
00:00:53,339 --> 00:00:54,880
down, so when it happened, you'd know the cross

22
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:55,780
was no accident.

23
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:57,340
It was the plan.

24
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:02,460
The suffering man of Psalm 22 has a name, Jesus.

25
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:05,980
They rolled dice for the clothes off his back,

26
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:09,400
never seeing what he was really doing, laying

27
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:12,240
down his life to win you back.
